      "id": 11447,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-10-23T15:05:26.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Playing Sentinel Tactics, The Wraith is attacking Baron Blade with a 4-die attack, and aiming. One of the attacks is a 6, so she ends up with four 6s.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Baron Blade rolls his three defense dice -- All 6s. I stare at it in disbelief. I mean, through all the years of rolling up D&amp;D characters, in particular, and all sorts of other games, I don't know if I've ever seen that -- a natural 18.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Then I notice that Blade has out his power that allows him another defense die and roll it. Another six.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Then I notice that The Wraith has out her power that allows her to reroll a defender's defense die. Another six.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A 4-die, aimed attack resulting in four sixes, plus the ability to reroll a defense die. All blocked.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:45.437Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
